<title>USA: NetLive, May Davis clash over directors.</title>
<headline>NetLive, May Davis clash over directors.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>NetLive Communications Inc said Friday it would &quot;vigorously resist&quot; efforts by its former underwriter, May Davis Group Inc. to unseat its board of directors through a consent solicitation.</p>
<p>NetLive also said that it intends to take legal action against May Davis and certain of its associates.</p>
<p>NetLive said that the May Davis efforts were part of an attempt to have the company acquired by the Zodiac Group Inc, a telephone entertainment network with revenues from psychic telephone lines and other telephone entertainment, and that a merger with Zodiac was not in the best interest of shareholders. (c) Reuters Limited 1997</p>
